2. Running and redistributing the original miner

You may run the unmodified miner, including for commercial or for-profit mining.
You may copy and redistribute its unmodified source and binaries if you retain
this license, NOTICE, LICENSING.md, all applicable third-party notices, and the
project credit and link specified in section 4. No mining fee or royalty is
created by this license.

Merely running this miner, invoking it through its documented process or
network interfaces, or distributing an unchanged copy alongside independent
software does not incorporate its code into that independent software.

3. Source-sharing requirement; no closed-source incorporation

You may study, modify, compile and incorporate Covered Code only subject to
this section and section 4. You may not copy, adapt, translate, link or embed
Covered Code, including compiled GPU kernels, into a closed-source miner,
library, application or other program without separate written permission
from its copyright holder.

A program incorporating Covered Code must make its complete Corresponding
Source publicly available, without a fee or access restriction, under terms
that permit recipients to inspect, use, modify and redistribute that source.
The source-sharing obligation and the attribution requirements of this
license must continue to apply to the Covered Code and modifications of it.
You must provide a prominent link to that source wherever the incorporating
program is distributed or offered for others to use. When supplying binaries,
provide the source for that exact version, not only an unrelated development
branch. Offering an incorporating program as a hosted service does not remove
these obligations.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for modifying the incorporating
program, including its modifications, GPU kernel sources, and scripts needed
to build and install it. It excludes private keys, credentials, user data,
model weights licensed separately, and unmodified general-purpose operating
systems, GPU drivers, compilers and independently supplied system libraries.
Their separate licenses remain applicable. Publishing only headers, an API,
obfuscated code, or precompiled kernels does not satisfy this requirement.

You may not grant downstream recipients permission to incorporate Covered Code
into a closed-source program. Commercial source-sharing programs are permitted
if they satisfy these conditions. A separate written license may grant an
exception; public availability of this repository is not such an exception.

4. Required credits and backlinks

Every incorporating program and its source distribution must retain the
relevant copyright and modification notices and include this credit:

  Includes code and/or GPU kernels from keryx-miner-supr by ocminer / Suprnova.
  https://github.com/ocminer/keryx-miner-supr

Place the credit and link prominently in the source repository's main README
and in the distributed program's accompanying credits or notices. If the
program provides an About, Credits or legal-notices screen or command, include
them there as well. Use a clickable backlink where the medium supports links;
a legible full URL is sufficient in plain text. Preserve this license and
NOTICE with the Covered Code. Clearly identify your own modifications without
implying endorsement by ocminer / Suprnova or the upstream authors.

